  "worked_solution": "If the number of copies remaining in stock is $N,$ then the rate of change of the number of copies is $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince $27$ copies are sold each day, the rate of change of the number of copies is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-27.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the number of copies remaining is *decreasing*.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
